  "title": "Classic Hot Dog",
  "subtitle": "All-beef frankfurter with mustard, ketchup, and onion",
  "excerpt": "A classic American hot dog is a beef frankfurter in a soft split roll, topped with yellow mustard, ketchup, and finely chopped onion. Simple assembly but the quality of the frankfurter matters: use a good all-beef frankfurter rather than a cheap mixed-meat sausage. Grilling or pan-frying gives a better result than boiling.",
