  "sourceNotes": "The hot dog as a street food is associated with New York, where German immigrants sold frankfurter sausages from pushcarts from the 1860s onward. The standardised combination of frankfurter, split roll, and condiments became ubiquitous at American sporting events and fairgrounds by the early 20th century.",
